msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:8
msgid "`nix version` - show the Nix version"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:12
msgid "`nix version` \\[_option_...\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:16
msgid "Show the Nix version:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:23
msgid ""
"Show the version together with the versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, as machine-readable JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:26
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix version --json\n"
"{\n"
"  \"version\": \"X.Y.Z\",\n"
"  \"libraries\": {\n"
"    \"libcurl\": \"P.Q.R\",\n"
"    \"libgit2\": \"A.B.C\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:37
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:39
msgid "Print the version of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:41
msgid ""
"Without any flags, this is like the [`nix --version`](../../command-ref/opt-"
"common.md#opt-version) option."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:44
msgid ""
"This subcommand additionally reports the versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against (see `--json` below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:46
msgid "With `--json`, the output is a JSON object with the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:48
msgid ""
"`version`: The version of Nix, as also printed by [`nix --version`](../../"
"command-ref/opt-common.md#opt-version)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:51
msgid ""
"`libraries`: An object mapping the names of Nix's direct third-party "
"dependencies to their versions. Which entries appear here depends on how Nix "
"was built, so consumers should not assume any particular key is present."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:56
msgid ""
"For a library that exposes its version at runtime, this is the version of "
"the loaded library, which _on some platforms_ may differ from the version "
"Nix was compiled against. For dependencies without such a query, it is the "
"version Nix was compiled with."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:61
msgid ""
"This list covers direct dependencies only; transitive dependencies are not "
"included."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md:64
